null,"evidence":["The plan enumerates only three of four states: 'declaration present + proof absent raises', 'Both markers absent = ... today's behaviour', and (implicitly) both-present = happy path.","The fourth state — declaration marker absent on root but proof marker present on the volume — can arise if user_data.sh writes the volume proof but the root declaration write fails or an operator removes it; the plan gives no rule for it.","Under the two stated rules this quadrant falls through to today's no-op behaviour (fail open), which is likely the intended benign resolution but is not stated, leaving the implementer to guess."],"finding":"The refusal state matrix leaves the declaration-absent + proof-present quadrant unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9eba90195266da33","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design — 'The refusal (AC3's teeth)'; AC line 4","norm_id":"naddac1f0ec63dd79","priority":0.2053,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["user_data.sh writes `<mount>/.gate-scratch-mounted` on the volume, then the write of `<mount>/../.gate-scratch-required` on root fails or is later deleted by an operator during recovery."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify that only 'declaration present AND proof absent' refuses, and every other combination (including proof-present-without-declaration) resolves to today's behaviour; add this quadrant to the no-op test case.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the RETIRE/cleanup path for scratch contents (who deletes stale reviewbot-* clones and aged gate snapshots), or cite the existing S6/review-bot mechanism that already reclaims them, so the isolated volume cannot silently accumulate to the 85% alarm.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the review-bot's per-review reviewbot-* clones' — these are created per review","'S6 bounds concurrent gates at 4, so 50 GiB leaves ~42 GiB below the 85% alarm'","ABSENCE: the plan defines CREATE (user_data formats/mounts, review-bot writes clones/snapshots) and CONSUME (gate_admission) but no statement of who deletes stale reviewbot-* clones or aged snapshots, nor whether that cleanup already exists upstream"],"finding":"The plan introduces a shared scratch volume consumed by up to 4 concurrent gates and per-review reviewbot-* clones, but specifies no RETIRE/cleanup path for the scratch CONTENTS (stale reviewbot-* clones and old gate snapshots). Sizing headroom + an 85% alarm is capacity monitoring, not retirement — without a cleanup owner the dedicated volume can accumulate to the 85% alarm and re-create a scaled-down version of the wedge it was built to prevent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"febcbab29c8f997b6","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design — Container / Sizing; AC line 5 (alarms)","norm_id":"n274a6a487e5c7c0e","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to the Design/Sizing section confirming the existing per-review clone teardown and snapshot-store eviction already bound scratch residency on the volume (or naming the cleanup this story adds), so RETIRE is not left implicit.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["prerequisite-consistency"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["S1: 'Default 50 GiB ... It is a variable, per ADR 0112 decision 6.'","S0 ADR Decision section contains only numbered items 1, 2, and 3."],"finding":"S1 cites 'ADR 0112 decision 6' as authority for making the scratch volume size a variable, but the finalized ADR 0112 (this prerequisite) enumerates exactly three numbered decisions (1: per-accumulator hard caps; 2: dedicated EBS scratch volume; 3: keep 60 GiB root as headroom). There is no decision 6 in the ADR text, so S1's citation cannot be satisfied by the prerequisi